\item \textbf{4. A Federal Reserve Exception: \textit{Trump v.\ Cook}, 609 U.S.\ \_\_\_ (2026).} Denying the government's application for a stay in Governor Lisa Cook's challenge to her removal, the Court held 5--4 (June 29, 2026) that the protection from removal enjoyed by Governors of the Federal Reserve is consistent with the Constitution, grounding that conclusion in the founding-era independence of the First Bank of the United States, and that Cook was entitled to notice of the charges and an opportunity to respond before any for-cause removal. Chief Justice Roberts wrote for the Court; Justices Thomas, Alito, Gorsuch, and Barrett dissented.
